   "source": [
    "____HYPERPARAMETER TUNING:-\n",
    "\n",
    "- we have different parameters for the modle.\n",
    "\n",
    "- here we pick a parameter that we can tune later to remove the overfitting from the data set.\n",
    "\n",
    "- examole:-\n",
    "\n",
    " 1.in simple linar regression --- we have straight line equation as,\n",
    "    y=B0 + B1X1 + c \n",
    "        where, B0 and B1X1 are the slope (cofficient), and c is the residual.\n",
    "    here, we will pick slope as the parameter that can be tuned later.\n",
    "    Because, slope is the important parameter here as due to overfitting the best fit line will get mold .\n",
    "\n",
    "2. in multi linear regression --- y = B0 + B1X1 + B2X2 + --- + BnXn + E\n",
    "    here , B0 , B1X1 , B2X2 and BnXn are slope and E is the residual/error/bias.\n",
    "    Here,  the parameter to be tuned will be slope.\n",
    "but we can also pick E as the tuned parameter as the error rate dosent have to be 100% accurate ,but we usually avoid it as we dont have any control on the error.\n",
    "\n",
    "- it has two works first to remove overfitting and second we can also tune the parameters that can help in increasing the accuracy later.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
